From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:34:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] aidl: Rust backend for framework AIDL: Java-only types,
 permission hook

--rust_java_type NAME=RUST_TYPE lets the Rust backend accept the Java-only
builtin NAME (Map, CharSequence, FileDescriptor, non-generic List) and
spell it RUST_TYPE; the caller supplies a Rust type that reads and writes
the Java backend bytes.

@EnforcePermission no longer fails Rust server stubs with compile_error!.
Like the Java backend's PermissionEnforcer, a fail-closed hook: an
interface with such methods gets EnforcePermission (Single / AllOf /
AnyOf, as parsed) and a required enforce_permission(method, permission)
on IFoo and IFooAsyncServer; the transaction calls it before reading
arguments and returns its Status without running the method on Err.
Wrappers forward it; the proxy, which serves nothing, denies.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ATL host tool: Rust services implement framework AIDL]
Patch-Reason: aidl rejects these types for non-Java backends in its type check (aidl_language.cpp LanguageSpecificCheckValid) and refuses permission-annotated Rust server methods in its code generation (generate_rust.cpp GenerateServerTransaction); no build config, environment or preprocessed declaration reaches either
---
